t. In it, two teenage boys who identify themselves only as \"Sphinx\" directly challenge the police, threatening to cause destruction and mayhem across Tokyo. Unable to stop the mass panic quickly spreading through the city and desperate for any leads in their investigation, the police struggle to act effectively against these terrorists, with Detective Kenjirou Shibazaki caught in the middle of it all.\n\nZankyou no Terror tells the story of Nine and Twelve, the two boys behind the masked figures of Sphinx. They should not exist, yet they stand strong in a world of deception and secrets while they make the city fall around them, all in the hopes of burying their own tragic truth.\n\n(Source: MAL Rewrite)"},"tags":[{"name":"Terrorism","rank":95,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Anti-Hero","rank":93,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Detective","rank":88,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Tragedy","rank":85,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Crime","rank":84,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":82,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Revenge","rank":81,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Orphan","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Urban","rank":73,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Police","rank":72,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Politics","rank":63,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Primarily Male Cast","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Female Protagonist","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Heterosexual","rank":60,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Human Experimentation","rank":60,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Mythology","rank":56,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Philosophy","rank":50,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Motorcycles","rank":46,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Suicide","rank":45,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Software Development","rank":41,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Guns","rank":40,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Time Skip","rank":20,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Shogi","rank":20,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Blackmail","rank":20,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"Terror in Resonance","english":"Terror in Resonance","native":"残響のテロル","romaji":"Zankyou no Terror","syno